/-! # Left injectivity in Jacobi-Zariski for an ind-etale final map

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tags 07D4 and 07D5, and the etale
specialization in lemma-henselization-NL
(blueprint: lem-sfb-ind-etale-jacobi-zariski-left-injective).

The canonical presentations are `Generators.self A B` and `Generators.self A C`.
Their differentials have free differential modules as their degree-zero terms.
Scalar extension is written with the scalar ring first, using tensor symmetry
with the node's convention. The ambient conormal formula specifies the restricted
map uniquely, so the existential conclusion does not leave the map arbitrary.
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u v w

namespace Algebra

/-- The canonical conormal map restricts to an injection from the kernel of the
termwise base-changed naive cotangent differential to `H1Cotangent A C`.
Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tags 07D4 and 07D5, with the etale
specialization used in lemma-henselization-NL
(blueprint: lem-sfb-ind-etale-jacobi-zariski-left-injective).

`Generators.defaultHom` between the self presentations fixes `A` and sends the
variable `[b]` to `[algebraMap B C b]`: the designated section of the target is
exactly its variable map. Thus `Cotangent.map` sends `[g]` to `[phi_sharp(g)]`,
and `liftBaseChange C` sends `c tensor [g]` to `c [phi_sharp(g)]`.
The source is the kernel after termwise tensoring, rather than a tensor product
of an already formed kernel. No locality, Noetherian or finite-presentation
assumption is made on `A` to `B`.

Proof for stage 3:
1. Choose a small filtered presentation of `C` by finitely presented etale
`B`-algebras `C_i` (def-weil-pbc-ind-etale-algebra). The affine etale criterion
(lem-weil-pbc-etale-ring-map-iff-etale-affine) and the etale clause of
lem-sfb-syntomic-smooth-composition make each stage syntomic. By
lem-sfb-syntomic-polynomial-kernel-koszul-regular, the kernel of a finite
polynomial presentation of `C_i` is locally generated by Koszul-regular sequences.
2. Put `P = A[B]` and `T = P[y_1,...,y_m]` for that finite presentation.
Let `L` be the kernel of `T` to `B[y_1,...,y_m]` and `K` that of `T` to `C_i`.
Apply lem-sfb-conormal-intersection-koszul-regular-ideal to get `L cap K^2 = L K`.
Then lem-weil-pbc-composed-conormal-injective-of-intersection injects the
base-changed conormal module into `K/K^2`. The differential square commutes
on polynomial generators, hence on all tensors, by
lem-weil-pbc-nl-presentation-h1-functoriality. Restrict to its differential kernel.
3. Map `T` to the canonical presentation `A[C_i]` on every variable by its
image in `C_i`. The homotopies of
lem-weil-pbc-nl-presentations-homotopy-equivalent identify the differential
kernels. Composing gives an injection `u_i`, with ambient formula
`c tensor [g]` sent to `c [phi_i_sharp(g)]`. These formulas on pure tensors
show compatibility with every transition map, by presentation functoriality.
4. Represent a cycle over `C` at a finite stage, using
lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-algebras-tensor-elementwise. Its differential is
eventually zero by the same lemma for the free differential module, so advance
to a stage where the representative is a cycle. If its canonical image is zero,
lem-sfb-filtered-colimit-naive-cotangent-comparison makes its class zero in the
colimit complex. The colimit of the `B`-algebras is also their colimit as
`A`-algebras, since the index is filtered and hence connected. There are no
terms in degree minus two, so a zero class in degree minus one is a zero element.
By lem-weil-pbc-filtered-colimit-modules-elementwise the conormal image is
therefore zero at a later stage. Compatibility and injectivity of `u_i` make
the cycle zero there, and hence zero over `C`. This proves injectivity of the
canonical restriction; no injective transitions or stagewise flatness is used. -/
theorem jacobiZariski_left_injective_of_indEtale
    (A : Type u) (B : Type v) (C : Type w)
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A B] [Algebra B C] [Algebra A C] [IsScalarTower A B C]
    (h : RingHom.IndEtaleAcrossUniverses (algebraMap B C)) :
    ∃ f : LinearMap.ker ((Generators.self A B).toExtension.cotangentComplex.baseChange C)
        →ₗ[C] H1Cotangent A C,
      (∀ x : LinearMap.ker
          ((Generators.self A B).toExtension.cotangentComplex.baseChange C),
        (Generators.self A C).toExtension.h1Cotangentι (f x) =
          (Extension.Cotangent.map
            (Generators.defaultHom (Generators.self A B)
              (Generators.self A C)).toExtensionHom).liftBaseChange C x.1) ∧
      Function.Injective f := by
  sorry

end Algebra
